ons\\\":[\\\"The downstream hazard I sourced (a later suffix request below the compacted index underflowing MemoryStorage's arithmetic) was not triggered: no promise or log-sync in this run asked for a prefix below the compacted index, so the over-compaction is witnessed with reads and the compacted index, not with a crash.\\\",\n   \\\"The baseline comparisons of this receipt are unknown because they were admitted through an event name shared with another case in the same execution; the pre-trim state is asserted from the sampled operands (events 9-11).\\\",\n   \\\"The drift and therefore the over-compaction were produced with three reconnection rounds and one leader change in a three-node cluster; other sizes, rounds and producers were not exercised.\\\",\n   \\\"No snapshot was created, so after the trim the entries were simply removed; whether a snapshot-enabled configuration would instead compact into a snapshot that no replica can serve was not exercised.\\\"]}],\n \\\"investigations\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":CH,\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"active\\\",\n  \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Whether a suffix or log-sync request below the compacted index occurs after an over-compaction (for example from a replica whose recorded accepted index is still truthful or from a freshly started instance), which MemoryStorage would evaluate as a subtraction below its compacted index; the decisive observation is a panic or a silently empty suffix on that path.\\\"}]}\njson.dump(up, open('update.json','w'), indent=1); print('written')\nPY\ntimeout 120 /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_09-22-17-omnipaxos-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -c 900\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
